# OWASP Security

Enforce these on every API route, Server Action, and form handler.

## Input Validation
Validate and sanitize at boundaries with Zod (or equivalent). Never trust client input.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const schema = z.object({ email: z.string().email(), name: z.string().min(1).max(100) });
const data = schema.parse(await request.json());
```

## Injection
Use ORM / parameterized queries only. Never concatenate user input into SQL, shell, or HTML.

## AuthZ / AuthN (BOLA/IDOR)
Check authentication **and** authorization server-side on every sensitive resource. Never rely on hidden UI alone.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — fetch by id from body without ownership check
// ✅ GOOD — session.userId must own resource.id before mutate/read
```

## Secrets & Data
- Never hardcode secrets; use env vars only.
- Never log passwords, tokens, PII, or full `.env` values.
- Don’t commit `.env` or credential files.

## Error Handling
Return generic client errors. Log details server-side only. Never expose stack traces, SQL, or infra paths to the client.

## XSS / CSRF
Escape/encode output; prefer framework defaults. Protect state-changing routes (SameSite cookies, CSRF tokens where needed).
